ision endoscopic imaging for screening colonoscopy: a prospective randomized trial</article-title><source><italic>Gastroenterology</italic></source><year>2009</year><volume>136</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>410</fpage><lpage>416</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">19014944</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B6"><label>6</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Uraoka</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Saito</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Matsuda</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Detectability of colorectal neoplastic lesions using a narrow-band imaging system: a pilot study</article-title><source><italic>Journal of Gastroenterology and Hepatology</italic></source><year>2008</year><volume>23</volume><issue>12</issue><fpage>1810</fpage><lpage>1815</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">19032454</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B7"><label>7</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rex</surname><given-names>DK</given-names></name><name><surname>Helbig</surname><given-names>CC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>High yields of small and flat adenomas with high-definition colonoscopes using either white light or narrow band imaging</article-title><source><italic>Gastroenterology</italic></source><year>2007</year><volume>133</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>42</fpage><lpage>47</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17631129</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B8"><label>8</label><element-citation publication-type="confproc"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>DaCosta</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name><name><surname>Lilge</surname><given-names>LD</given-names></name><name><surname>Kost</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Jacques</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Confocal fluorescence microscopy, microspectrofluorimetry, and modeling studies of laser-induced fluorescence endoscopy (LIFE) of human colon tissue</article-title><conf-name>In: Laser-Tissue Interaction VIII, vol. 2975</conf-name><conf-date>February 1997</conf-date><fpage>98</fpage><lpage>107</lpage><comment><italic>Proceedings of SPIE</italic>.</comment></element-citation></ref><ref id="B9"><label>9</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Izuishi</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Tajiri</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Fujii</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>The histological basis of detection of adenoma and cancer in the colon by autofluorescence endoscopic imaging</article-title><source><italic>Endoscopy</italic></source><year>1999</year><volume>31</volume><issue>7</issue><fpage>511</fpage><lpage>516</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10533733</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B10"><label>10</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Auler</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Banzer</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Untersuchungen &#x000fc;ber die rolle der porphyrine bei geschwulstkranken menschen und tieren</article-title><source><italic>Zeitschrift f&#x000fc;r Krebsforschung</italic></source><year>1942</year><volume>53</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>65</fpage><lpage>67</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="B11"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>VASSAR</surname><given-names>PS</given-names></name><name><surname>SAUNDERS</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>CULLIN